Dialogue: 1,0:00:33.40,0:00:38.40,Panel,,0,0,0,,{\pos(1448,820)}{\fad(1000,1000)}{\fs48\fsp2}Sato Hinata\N{\fs36\alpha&H30&}Voice of Mizuki Akiyama
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.01,0:00:26.45,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,Yep
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.39,0:00:32.99,Ena,,0,0,0,,Thank you, everyone, for writing in so many thoughtful comments about the story.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.24,0:00:33.25,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.99,0:00:36.77,Ena,,0,0,0,,So after watching all of that, we'd like to talk a little
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.77,0:00:42.44,Ena,,0,0,0,,about how we, as actors, decided to act out this story.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.44,0:00:47.98,Ena,,0,0,0,,and also, what we kept in mind as we performed during the actual recording.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.98,0:00:51.17,Ena,,0,0,0,,We hope that you take all of this to heart as you listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.17,0:00:54.74,Ena,,0,0,0,,Starting with Ena, in this Episode 8...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.62,0:00:57.39,Ena,,0,0,0,,Well, not just in Episode 8,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.39,0:01:05.52,Ena,,0,0,0,,considering all that's happened in the previous stories, when I try to put myself in Ena's shoes,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.52,0:01:09.00,Ena,,0,0,0,,I know there's no 100% correct answer,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.00,0:01:16.86,Ena,,0,0,0,,but what I do is think through how she might think and act.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.86,0:01:24.17,Ena,,0,0,0,,I'd think about this over and over as I pored over the script, putting myself in Ena's position.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.17,0:01:28.13,Ena,,0,0,0,,But here, in the last episode,...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.13,0:01:33.32,Ena,,0,0,0,,Actually, for me, not just in the event stories,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.32,0:01:36.73,Ena,,0,0,0,,but anytime I'm performing in general,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.73,0:01:40.00,Ena,,0,0,0,,I can kind of get carried away by the story's mood.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.00,0:01:43.00,Ena,,0,0,0,,And then, um, how should I put it,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.00,0:01:46.12,Ena,,0,0,0,,it just turns into tears and more tears.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.12,0:01:48.56,Ena,,0,0,0,,I'd just want to go there so bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.56,0:01:53.94,Ena,,0,0,0,,I get so emotionally moved and can't help but start crying too.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.94,0:01:58.00,Ena,,0,0,0,,And in the script too, the script for Episode 8
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.00,0:02:01.90,Ena,,0,0,0,,we always have lots of notes about how lines should be delivered.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.90,0:02:04.88,Ena,,0,0,0,,Stuff like "cry a bit here", or "sniffle a bit here".
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.88,0:02:06.71,Ena,,0,0,0,,Lots of small directions like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.71,0:02:14.72,Ena,,0,0,0,,Looking at that, I started thinking about how to play Ena crying in this scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.72,0:02:20.18,Ena,,0,0,0,,And so when Ena says "it's okay to be yourself", and "you're still loved the way you are,"
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.18,0:02:22.95,Ena,,0,0,0,,pouring her whole heart out to Mizuki,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.95,0:02:26.40,Ena,,0,0,0,,I came up with a whole plan on how she might say all that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.40,0:02:31.94,Ena,,0,0,0,,I wanted to act with those feelings coming from my own heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.94,0:02:35.72,Ena,,0,0,0,,But when I went to record my take,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.72,0:02:39.57,Ena,,0,0,0,,the director told me they wanted more of a "catfight" vibe.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.57,0:02:43.71,Ena,,0,0,0,,They said "we’d really like to see Mizuki and Ena have a catfight."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.71,0:02:49.62,Ena,,0,0,0,,And so I was like "Oh, so she doesn’t have to cry? She can fight instead?"
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.62,0:02:54.85,Ena,,0,0,0,,So as I kept thinking "what kind of Ena would that look like?", I suddenly realized,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.85,0:03:00.04,Ena,,0,0,0,,in the script, Ena says "my feelings haven't changed."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.04,0:03:05.83,Ena,,0,0,0,,My initial plan and all the directions in the script notes were really helpful,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.83,0:03:09.90,Ena,,0,0,0,,but that came from me treasuring Mizuki so much,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.90,0:03:13.90,Ena,,0,0,0,,that I started to think overprotectively of her.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.90,0:03:19.94,Ena,,0,0,0,,I felt that wasn't right. I felt that's not what Ena would do.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.94,0:03:24.73,Ena,,0,0,0,,Of course, that desire to care so so much for her is precious too,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.73,0:03:29.48,Ena,,0,0,0,,but it's precisely because Ena cares so much that she needs to vent her frustrations,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.48,0:03:31.41,Ena,,0,0,0,,and think "why don't you get it?"
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.41,0:03:38.37,Ena,,0,0,0,,Almost like that constant bickering they always get into is still important to Ena.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.28,0:03:45.12,Ena,,0,0,0,,When I look at the whole picture, as someone who isn't Ena, it seems like this grandiose affair.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.12,0:03:50.08,Ena,,0,0,0,,And while Mizuki really is the only one who fully understands her situation,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.08,0:03:53.08,Ena,,0,0,0,,to the two of them, to Ena,...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.08,0:03:57.17,Ena,,0,0,0,,it was just a simple squabble between friends. I think that's how Ena sees it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.72,0:04:03.58,Ena,,0,0,0,,For the two of us, looking from the outside in, we might see it as this huge incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.58,0:04:12.06,Ena,,0,0,0,,But I see this as the point where the Ena and Mizuki for the first time get to properly face each other after avoiding it until now.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.06,0:04:18.36,Ena,,0,0,0,,That was the understanding I performed with.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.36,0:04:28.33,Ena,,0,0,0,,So actually, I was a bit worried that the card art didn't quite match this furious Ena I was imagining,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.33,0:04:31.66,Ena,,0,0,0,,but I was really relieved that it turned out so wonderful.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.99,0:04:39.57,Ena,,0,0,0,,Right, so since we also have Mizuki with us here today,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.57,0:04:42.62,Ena,,0,0,0,,I'd love to hear your thoughts not only on this event's Episode 8,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.62,0:04:48.65,Ena,,0,0,0,,but also about the exchange between Ena and Mizuki in the last event's Episode 8.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.65,0:04:50.76,Ena,,0,0,0,,Do we have time for that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.67,0:04:53.71,Ena,,0,0,0,,I mean, for Mizuki...
Dialogue: 3,0:04:54.99,0:04:58.12,Ena,,0,0,0,,For Mizuki, both Episode 8s are still unmissable, aren't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.12,0:05:06.64,Ena,,0,0,0,,In the last Episode 8, Ena had a hard time finding the right words for Mizuki, and I think the same was true for me as well, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.64,0:05:09.07,Ena,,0,0,0,,What did you think, Hinata-chan?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.94,0:05:09.07,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.79,0:05:16.11,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,I... I don't think it's really my place to talk about what Mizuki might have been feeling.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.11,0:05:25.77,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,But on the technical side, for both the last event story, "Whither This Path of Thorns", and this one,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.77,0:05:32.10,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,I was a bit torn on whether to record the scenes standing up or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.10,0:05:39.91,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,I'm personally the type who needs to act with more than just my voice,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.91,0:05:46.05,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,so I thought standing, like on a stage, might help.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.05,0:05:56.47,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,But when you're crying, your legs naturally lose strength. So to focus solely on my voice, I decided it might be better to sit.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.47,0:06:10.48,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,In the last event "Whither This Path of Thorns" Episode 8, my initial plan was to try speaking clearly even through all the crying.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.48,0:06:16.69,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,But I was directed to cry even more, so we tried three or four more takes...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.69,0:06:20.87,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,Also, for both stories, I recorded my lines before ever hearing Minori-chan's,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.69,0:06:20.87,Note,,0,0,0,,{\pos(444.8,190.8)}(This Minori-chan, not MMJ)
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.87,0:06:25.50,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,so I only heard the full scenes at the same time as you all did.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.50,0:06:36.28,Mizuki,,0,0,0,,I saw just how well the whole final work came together, and I feel like I put my absolute best into it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.28,0:06:41.60,Ena,,0,0,0,,I mean, we actually did talk a lot, even if not during the recordings,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.60,0:06:45.84,Ena,,0,0,0,,like "how did you perform this part?", or "what were your directions for this part?"
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.84,0:06:50.27,Ena,,0,0,0,,If I could make a just a small request to the staff,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.27,0:06:58.15,Ena,,0,0,0,,one day maybe we could record our dialogues together in the same studio.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.15,0:07:03.82,Ena,,0,0,0,,I know the staff here at Project Sekai put a lot of care into our acting, so maybe next time...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.82,0:07:10.74,Ena,,0,0,0,,Maybe there's a chance to see a more grown-up Mizuki and Ena run into another challenge,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.74,0:07:13.34,Ena,,0,0,0,,and then one of them will have to help the other out.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.34,0:07:18.38,Ena,,0,0,0,,I think it would be great to see and record a scene like that sometime in the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.06,0:07:22.66,Ena,,0,0,0,,But for now, we're still so happy with how it all turned out.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.66,0:07:26.27,Ena,,0,0,0,,We were like "yay~" before this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.27,0:07:30.29,Ena,,0,0,0,,Alright, now then, we've talked for a while, so it's time for the next segment.
